{"id": "86236", "name": "משוואה ריבועית – פתרון בהשלמה לריבוע, מקדם מוביל 1 (באנגלית)", "defaultgrade": 1, "penalty": 0.1, "options": {"multiplicationsign": "none", "complexno": "i", "matrixparens": "[", "inversetrig": "cos-1", "logicsymbol": "lang", "sqrtsign": true}, "nhints": 0, "questiontext": "<div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"max-width:980px;font-family:Arial;line-height:1.7\"><div style=\"background:#F4F1F5;border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px\"><p>Solve the following quadratic equation by completing the square:</p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ {{CT:0}} = 0. \\]</p></div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:14px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><div style=\"font-weight:bold;color:#4b1f6f;margin-bottom:8px\"><span style=\"display:inline-block;width:26px;height:26px;line-height:26px;text-align:center;border-radius:50%;background:#4b1f6f;color:#fff;margin-right:8px\">a</span></div><p>Give the completed square form:</p><div style=\"background:#FAF9FB;border-radius:8px;padding:10px;direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate\">[[input:cans]] \\(=0.\\)</div><div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate;margin-top:6px\">[[validation:cans]]</div><div style=\"margin-top:6px\">[[feedback:comp]]</div></div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:14px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><div style=\"font-weight:bold;color:#4b1f6f;margin-bottom:8px\"><span style=\"display:inline-block;width:26px;height:26px;line-height:26px;text-align:center;border-radius:50%;background:#4b1f6f;color:#fff;margin-right:8px\">b</span></div><p>Hence solve the quadratic, giving your answer as a set \\(\\left(\\mbox e.g.\\ \\left\\{x_1 , x_2\\right\\} \\right)\\):</p><div style=\"background:#FAF9FB;border-radius:8px;padding:10px;direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate\">\\({{CT:1}} \\in \\) [[input:ans]]</div><div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate;margin-top:6px\">[[validation:ans]]</div><p class=\"input-hint input-hint-root\" dir=\"ltr\" style=\"font-size:0.88em;color:#555;margin:6px 0 0;text-align:left\">How to enter: a square root as <code dir=\"ltr\">sqrt(...)</code>, e.g. <code dir=\"ltr\">sqrt(5*x)</code>. Other roots as a power, with brackets around the exponent: \\(\\sqrt[3]{x+1}\\) is entered as <code dir=\"ltr\">(x+1)^(1/3)</code>.</p><div style=\"margin-top:6px\">[[feedback:prt1]]</div></div></div>", "generalfeedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"max-width:980px;font-family:Arial;line-height:1.7\"><div style=\"background:#F4F1F5;border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:12px 16px;margin-bottom:12px\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Outline:</b> Complete the square to remove the first-degree term, isolate the square, take the square root with \\(\\pm\\), and solve for the variable.</div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:12px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Step 1 — The method</b><br>When solving a more complicated quadratic a better option, than factorising, is completing the square (The method by which we remove the {{CT:2}} term). The general rule (when the \\(x^2\\) coefficient is one) is:<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ x^2+ax+b = \\left(x+\\frac{a}{2} \\right)^2-\\frac{a^2}{4}+b. \\]</p>Once you have removed the \\(x\\) term you can rearrange the formula to find \\((x+\\frac{a}{2})^2\\). Then you simply need to square root and rearrange to find \\(x\\).</div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:12px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Step 2 — Completing the square (part a)</b><br>In this example:<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ {{CT:0}} = 0, \\]</p>we complete the square:<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ {{CT:3}} = 0. \\]</p></div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:12px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Step 3 — Taking the square root</b><br>Rearranging gives:<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ {{CT:4}} = {{CT:5}}. \\]</p>Square root (remember to take plus and minus):<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ {{CT:6}} = \\pm {{CT:7}}. \\]</p></div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:12px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Step 4 — The solution set (part b)</b><br>Finally:<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ {{CT:1}} = {{CT:8}} \\pm {{CT:7}}. \\]</p>Therefore, our solution set is:<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ {{CT:1}} \\in \\left\\{ {{CT:9}} , {{CT:10}}    \\right\\}. \\]</p></div></div>", "specificfeedback": "", "prtcorrect": "<span class='correct'>Correct answer, well done.</span>", "prtpartiallycorrect": "<span class='partially'>Your answer is partially correct.</span>", "prtincorrect": "<span class='incorrect'>Incorrect answer.</span>", "inputs": [{"name": "ans", "type": "algebraic", "boxsize": 15, "insertstars": 0, "forbidfloat": true, "forbidwords": "", "allowwords": "", "mustverify": true, "showvalidation": 1, "syntaxhint": "", "syntaxattribute": 0, "options": "", "requirelowestterms": true}, {"name": "cans", "type": "algebraic", "boxsize": 15, "insertstars": 0, "forbidfloat": true, "forbidwords": "", "allowwords": "", "mustverify": true, "showvalidation": 1, "syntaxhint": "", "syntaxattribute": 0, "options": "", "requirelowestterms": true}], "prts": [{"name": "comp", "value": 1, "autosimplify": true, "feedbackstyle": 1, "feedbackvariables": "", "firstnode": 0, "nodes": [{"name": 0, "answertest": "CompSquare", "sans": "cans", "tans": "cta", "testoptions": "v", "quiet": false, "on_true": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 1, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "comp-0-T ", "feedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\"><b>Part a — correct.</b></div>"}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "comp-0-F ", "feedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\"><b>Part a — incorrect.</b> Write the quadratic as \\((x+p)^2+q\\): \\(p\\) is half the coefficient of the first-degree term, and \\(q\\) makes the constant term right.</div>"}}]}, {"name": "prt1", "value": 1, "autosimplify": true, "feedbackstyle": 1, "feedbackvariables": "", "firstnode": 0, "nodes": [{"name": 0, "answertest": "AlgEquiv", "sans": "ans", "tans": "{ta1, ta2 }", "testoptions": null, "quiet": false, "on_true": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 1, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "1-0-T ", "feedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\"><b>Part b — correct.</b></div>"}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": 1, "answernote": "1-0-F ", "feedback": ""}}, {"name": 1, "answertest": "AlgEquiv", "sans": "ans", "tans": "{?,?}", "testoptions": null, "quiet": false, "on_true": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "1-1-T ", "feedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\">Replace the question marks with the solutions to the quadratic.</div>"}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "1-1-F ", "feedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\"><b>Part b — incorrect.</b> Isolate the square from part a, take the square root (both signs) and solve.</div>"}}]}], "qvnames": ["a", "b", "cta", "ta1", "ta2", "v"], "nvariants": 50}